\par\par \b \uc2 UPDATE 1- \highlight22\uc2 Ukraine \highlight\uc2  cbank to switch to auctions from  \highlight22\uc2 intervention \highlight\b0\par\par\uc2 334 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 7 September 2009\par 17:45\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2009 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 (Combines stories, adds details)\par \par \uc2 KIEV, Sept 7 (Reuters) - \b \highlight22\uc2 Ukraine\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  will stop \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  on the interbank market at a fixed rate, but will carry out auctions at which it is willing to sell $1 billion in September, Chairman Volodymyr Stelmakh said on Monday.\par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 hryvnia currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  has lost almost 15 percent in the past two months, while the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  last \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  last Tuesday, refraining from \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  last Thursday and Monday, as it normally would have.\par \par \uc2 "As of tomorrow, we will move to a new system of participation on the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market -- auctions. This means that we will sell to whoever bids the highest," Stelmakh told journalists.\par \par \uc2 He said the bank would spend about $1 billion on supporting the \b \highlight22\uc2 hryvnia\b0 \highlight\uc2 , which is the average amount it has spent every month since January.\par \par \uc2 Since the start of the year, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  on Mondays, Tuesdays and Thursdays and carried out foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  auctions on Wednesdays and Fridays.\par \par \uc2 "We will carry auctions as often as our previous \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2 ," Stelmakh said, but without confirmation how many days a week and what if anything would take place the current \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  auctions on Wednesdays and Fridays.\par \par \uc2 Stelmakh also said the government's 2010 budget was calculated at a \b \highlight22\uc2 hryvnia\b0 \highlight\uc2  rate of 8.5-8.6/$, though he declined to give his own forecast for the \b \highlight22\uc2 hryvnia\b0 \highlight\uc2  next year.\par \par \uc2 The finance ministry had said before it would prepare the budget based on the \b \highlight22\uc2 hryvnia\b0 \highlight\uc2 's current rate because the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  had not given its forecast for the \b \highlight22\uc2 hryvnia\b0 \highlight\uc2  next year.\par \par \uc2 "It has already been announced that next year's budget is calculated at a rate of 8.5-8.6 \b \highlight22\uc2 hryvnias\b0 \highlight\uc2  a dollar," Stelmakh said.\par \par \uc2 He also said, Ukraine's total foreign debt obligations to the end of the year stand at $1.9 billion. (Reporting by Natalya Zinets; Editing by Ron Askew)\par \par \uc2 UKRAINE-CBANK/ (UPDATE 1)|LANGEN|ABN|M|D|BNX   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020090907e5970013y\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
