\par\par \b \uc2 Ukrainians queue for dlrs as cbank  \highlight22\uc2 intervenes \highlight\b0\par\par\uc2 471 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 28 August 2009\par 17:24\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2009 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 KIEV, Aug 28 (Reuters) - \b \highlight22\uc2 Ukraine\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  injected over $250 million this week into the cash \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market through \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  but long queues formed at banks on Friday as ordinary people clamoured for the dollar.\par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 hryvnia currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  has lost over 10 percent of its value to the dollar in the past two months, trading at about 8.5/$ this week from 7.7/$ at the start of July as the state and banks have to pay more foreign debt than before and imports rise.\par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 hryvnia\b0 \highlight\uc2 's fall has been far slower than the plunge of about 30 percent last December alone when the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  hit a historic low of 9.5-10/$. But this time, even the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has acknowledged that Ukrainians were "panicked" by the rate.\par \par \uc2 The bank, which has been \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  or conducting foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  auctions practically every day since the start of the year, limited its sales of the dollar this week to banks needing to supply their foreign cash exchange booths.\par \par \uc2 "This had to be done to clam people down. When we saw the panicked mood, we sold $92 million the day before yesterday (Tuesday) and $170 million today (Thursday)," First Deputy Chairman Anatoly Shapovalov told a talk show late on Thursday.\par \par \uc2 However, not all banks managed to buy the dollars from the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  and that meant those who were successful sold dollars on Friday at 8.1/$ and those who were not, at 8.5/$.\par \par \uc2 One of the conditions of the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  has been that the cash sale rate should be no more than 2 percent above the \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  rate.\par \par \uc2 Long queues formed throughout the day outside banks with the cheaper rate.\par \par \uc2 Shapovalov said the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  had spent $8 billion on \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  since the start of the year, including $1.12 billion in July alone when the \b \highlight22\uc2 hryvnia\b0 \highlight\uc2  started slipping.\par \par \uc2 That is worth a quarter of the bank's reserves as they stood at the beginning of this month. But Shapovalov said the volumes do not break any conditions set by the International Monetary Fund with which Kiev has a $16.4 billion loan programme.\par \par \uc2 "We have a programme with the IMF, which has been signed by all the leaders in the government... \b \highlight22\uc2 Intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  is being carried within the limits (set by the IMF)," Shapovalov said.\par \par \uc2 The IMF has already disbursed $10.6 billion of the total since November, including $3.3 billion last month. But that last tranche went directly to the government to plug a hole in its budget and pay external debts. "This has reduced our possibility to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  by $3.3 billion," Shapovalov said. (Reporting by Natalya Zinets; writing by Sabina Zawadzki; editing by Toby Chopra)\par \par \uc2 UKRAINE-\b \highlight22\uc2 CURRENCY\b0 \highlight\uc2 /|LANGEN|ABN|M|D   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020090831e58s0015k\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
