\par\par \b \uc2 UPDATE 1- \highlight22\uc2 Ukraine \highlight\uc2  cbank  \highlight22\uc2 intervenes \highlight\uc2 ,  \highlight22\uc2 hryvnia \highlight\uc2  seen lower\b0\par\par\uc2 369 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 25 August 2009\par 12:29\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2009 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 (Adds \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  notice, analyst, details)\par \par \uc2 KIEV, Aug 25 (Reuters) - \b \highlight22\uc2 Ukraine\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  weakened its \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  rate, selling dollars at 8.0 \b \highlight22\uc2 hryvnias\b0 \highlight\uc2  on Tuesday, against 7.95 \b \highlight22\uc2 hryvnias\b0 \highlight\uc2  last Thursday, bank data showed.\par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  limited sales of dollars to banks for use on the cash market. It later told banks in a notice it would \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  on Thursday with the same limits -- but did not give a sell rate.\par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  reminded banks that they should not sell dollars on the cash market at rates higher than 2 percent above its \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  rate and could only sell 8,000 \b \highlight22\uc2 hryvnias\b0 \highlight\uc2 -worth (about $1,000) of dollars per person per day.\par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 hryvnia\b0 \highlight\uc2  was trading little changed on Tuesday at 8.4-8.5/$. It has fallen over 3 percent in value against the dollar in August and the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  said last Friday that was mainly due to payments for imports and foreign debts.\par \par \uc2 But on Monday it said the "destabilisation on the foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market is due to the cash market".\par \par \uc2 Banks sold $2.5 billion to Ukrainians on the cash market in July and bought back $1.4 billion, when the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  spent $1.1 billion on \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has been \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  or carrying out foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  auctions practically every day this year after the \b \highlight22\uc2 hryvnia\b0 \highlight\uc2  lost over 60 percent of its value in the last months of 2008, hitting a historic low of almost 10/$ in December.\par \par \uc2 It normally \b \highlight22\uc2 intervenes\b0 \highlight\uc2  on Mondays, Tuesdays and Thursdays and carries out foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  auctions on Wednesdays and Fridays. Analysts and dealers said despite that, they saw no reason for the \b \highlight22\uc2 hryvnia\b0 \highlight\uc2  to strengthen soon.\par \par \uc2 "We have Eurobond payments to make in August and September and then we will begin payments for syndicated loans and on top of that gas will have to be stored soon," said Mikhail Salnikov, analyst at investment fund Sokrat.\par \par \uc2 "This all increases the demand for the dollar and raises its rate (to the \b \highlight22\uc2 hryvnia\b0 \highlight\uc2 )," he said. (Reporting by Natalya Zinets; Writing by Sabina Zawadzki; editing by Chris Pizzey)\par \par \uc2 UKRAINE-\b \highlight22\uc2 CURRENCY\b0 \highlight\uc2 / (UPDATE 1)|LANGEN|ABN|M|D   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020090828e58p000tn\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
