\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 Ukraine \highlight\uc2  c.bank alters Thursday sell  \highlight22\uc2 intervention \highlight\uc2  rate\b0\par\par\uc2 200 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 3 Juni 2009\par 18:12\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2009 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 KIEV, June 3 (Reuters) - \b \highlight22\uc2 Ukraine\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  said on Wednesday it would sell dollars at 7.63 \b \highlight22\uc2 hryvnias\b0 \highlight\uc2  in its Thursday \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , compared to 7.65 on Tuesday but leaving its "buy" rate unchanged at 7.61.\par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  did not \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  on the interbank market on Wednesday, but sold dollars at auction at 7.63 \b \highlight22\uc2 hryvnias\b0 \highlight\uc2 . The \b \highlight22\uc2 hryvnia\b0 \highlight\uc2  traded on the interbank market at 7.58 to 7.65.\par \par \uc2 After months of propping the \b \highlight22\uc2 hryvnia\b0 \highlight\uc2  by selling dollars through \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  and auctions, the bank has in recent weeks begun operating on both the sell and buy side.\par \par \uc2 The daily action in support of the \b \highlight22\uc2 hryvnia\b0 \highlight\uc2  enabled the Ukrainian \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  to claw back some ground after losing 60 percent of its value from October to late February.\par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  last week said reserves had risen for the first time since November, jumping by around $3.3 billion due to the second tranche of an IMF loan and \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  purchases by the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  -- totalling $133 million last month. (Reporting by Natalya Zinets, writing by Ron Popeski; editing by Patrick Graham)\par \