\par\par \b \uc2 UPDATE 1- \highlight22\uc2 Ukraine \highlight\uc2  C.Bank cuts spending on  \highlight22\uc2 intervention \highlight\b0\par\par\uc2 430 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 6 April 2009\par 14:55\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2009 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 (adds \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  rates for Tuesday, para 6)\par \par \uc2 KIEV, April 6 (Reuters) - \b \highlight22\uc2 Ukraine\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  said on Monday its spending of reserves to prop up the \b \highlight22\uc2 hryvnia currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  against its sharp falls of recent months, had declined 38 percent in March compared to the previous month.\par \par \uc2 A \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  statement said it had spent $1.077 billion in March against $1.73 billion in February on \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  and sale of dollars at auctions.\par \par \uc2 Spending in the first quarter of 2009 was $4.418 billion, 57 percent down from $10.284 billion in the last quarter of 2008.\par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 hryvnia\b0 \highlight\uc2  has lost 60 percent of its value against the U.S. dollar since last September in Ukraine, but clawed back 1.7 percent in March. \b \highlight22\uc2 Central bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  has sought to help borrowers meet foreign debt requirements in difficult conditions of obtaining credits and an outflow of funds from the country.\par \par \uc2 "The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  has reduced the shortage of foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  on the domestic market," the bank said, noting how the \b \highlight22\uc2 hryvnia\b0 \highlight\uc2  gained ground on the interbank market last month.\par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  later said it would offer to sell dollars at 7.9 \b \highlight22\uc2 hryvnias\b0 \highlight\uc2  on Tuesday and buy at 7.70, rates that have in place for more than month.\par \par \uc2 The dollar traded on Monday on the interbank market at 8.12/8.25.\par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  generally \b \highlight22\uc2 intervenes\b0 \highlight\uc2  three or four times a week, selling dollars at advantageous rates to buyers needing to repay debts, and has also begun organising auctions for dollars and other \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  once or twice a week.\par \par \uc2 It says the introduction of auctions has cut demand for foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  significantly.\par \par \uc2 The bank said the \b \highlight22\uc2 hryvnia\b0 \highlight\uc2 's average rate to the dollar, calculated on the basis of all transactions on the interbank market, rose in March to 7.9743 from 8.108 in February.\par \par \uc2 Dealers say demand for foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  has fallen because imports have declined in conditions of economic crisis, regular \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  and the prospect of restored credits from the International Monetary Fund.\par \par \uc2 An IMF mission is due to return to Kiev this week to discuss resuming credits under a $16.4 billion loan -- suspended in a disagreement over reforms.\par \par \uc2 Dealers also say restrictions on who may purchase dollars and regulations aimed to change the structure of banks' open \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  positions have also propped the \b \highlight22\uc2 hryvnia\b0 \highlight\uc2 . (Reporting by Natalya Zinets, writing by Ron Popeski, editing by Victoria Main)\par \par \uc2 UKRAINE-\b \highlight22\uc2 CURRENCY\b0 \highlight\uc2 / (UPDATE 1)|LANGEN|ABN|M|E|RBN|D|RNP   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020090406e546001l1\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\pics