\par\par \b \uc2 UPDATE 1- \highlight22\uc2 Ukraine central bank \highlight\uc2  auctions dollars, euros\b0\par\par\uc2 339 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 20 M\u228\'00\'E4rz 2009\par 16:36\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2009 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 (adds \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  rates for Monday, para 6)\par \par \uc2 KIEV, March 20 (Reuters) - \b \highlight22\uc2 Ukraine\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  said on Friday it intended to sell dollars at 7.8 \b \highlight22\uc2 hryvnias\b0 \highlight\uc2  and euros at 10.66 at its weekly auction of hard \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  funds.\par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has sought to strengthen its hold over the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  since December after the \b \highlight22\uc2 hryvnia\b0 \highlight\uc2  tumbled in the final months of 2008 on rising bank problems, a collapsing steel sector and growing worries over Ukraine's solvency.\par \par \uc2 Since the start of the year the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has tried to keep the rate at around 7.7 per dollar, well below the 2008 peak around 4.5 per euro.\par \par \uc2 At its last auction, it sold $68.6 million at a rate of 7.8 \b \highlight22\uc2 hryvnias\b0 \highlight\uc2  and 1.01 million euros at 9.97 \b \highlight22\uc2 hryvnias\b0 \highlight\uc2  -- its first such auction of the European \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Participation is limited to banks presenting a calendar of payments in March for individuals or small businesses. The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  said banks had set aside 368.8 million \b \highlight22\uc2 hryvnias\b0 \highlight\uc2  for the purchase of \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  later announced it would \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  on the interbank market on Monday, buying dollars at 7.7 and selling at 7.9 -- rates which have varied little over the past month.\par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervenes\b0 \highlight\uc2  from Monday to Thursday in support of the \b \highlight22\uc2 hryvnia\b0 \highlight\uc2 , offering to sell dollars at what amounts to discounted rates. It holds auctions on Fridays, also at rates more favourable to buyers than on the interbank market.\par \par \uc2 Exchange offices were offering to sell dollars on Friday at about 8.5 and euros at 11.7.\par \par \uc2 Banks have been reluctant to post \b \highlight22\uc2 hryvnia\b0 \highlight\uc2  rates in view of warnings from the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  that they would face punitive measures if the figures differed significantly from an "average" rate calculated from the previous day's transactions. (Reporting by Natalya Zinets, writing by Ron Popeski; Editing by Marius Zaharia/Ruth Pitchford)\par \par \uc2 UKRAINE-\b \highlight22\uc2 CURRENCY\b0 \highlight\uc2 / (UPDATE 1)|LANGEN|ABN|M|D   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020090320e53k001fe\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
