\par\par \b \uc2 EMERGING MARKETS-Shares down as emerging Europe  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2  weaken\b0\par\par\uc2 759 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 24 Februar 2009\par 13:30\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2009 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 * Emerging shares fall to 11-week lows on global selloff\par \par \uc2 * South African markets hit by GDP data\par \par \uc2 * Emerging Europe \b \highlight22\uc2 FX\b0 \highlight\uc2  selling pressure resumes\par \par \uc2 * Ukraine \b \highlight22\uc2 hryvnia\b0 \highlight\uc2  continues slide on IMF aid suspension\par \par \uc2 By Sebastian Tong and Martina Fuchs\par \par \uc2 LONDON, Feb 24 (Reuters) - Emerging shares sank nearly 2 percent on Tuesday amid a global selloff sparked off by renewed fears over the financial system while central European \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  weakened a day after joint verbal \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  from the region's central bankers offered brief respite.\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Ukraine\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 hryvnia currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  continued its slide as an IMF aid programme remained suspended, while South African markets came under pressure after figures showed its economy shrinking for the first time in a decade in the fourth quarter of 2008.\par \par \uc2 Investors are growing nervous that the various bailout packages unveiled by governments around the world may not be enough to stabilise the global banking sector as Washington mulled a possible increase in its stake in \uc2 Citigroup\uc2  and insurer AIG looks to more state funds.\par \par \uc2 A wave of global selling knocked world stocks <.MIWD00000PUS> to their lowest since April 2003, sending Wall Street to 12-year lows on Monday. However, emerging equity losses were more modest with the benchmark index <.MSCIEF> down to its lowest level since Dec. 5.\par \par \uc2 By 1145 GMT, the key emerging share index was down 1.66 percent to 501.67 while emerging sovereign debt spreads <11EMJ> widened 3 basis points to trade at 674 bps above U.S. Treasuries.\par \par \uc2 "Emerging Europe is suffering more than many Asian or Latin American countries. The region is getting hit by the global trade shock and directly by the credit crunch, as the banks don't want to lend. Markets seem to be wanting to price this in as quickly as possible," said Charlie Robertson, chief Europe, Middle East and Asia economist at ING.\par \par \uc2 Among the day's biggest equity losers were Romania <.BETI> and Poland <.WIG20>, which saw their bourses fall over 2 percent.\par \par \uc2 South African shares suffered the largest falls with the key index <.JTOPI> down nearly 3 percent following data showing a bigger-than-expected contraction in South Africa's economy in the fourth quarter. [ID:nLO6887]\par \par \uc2 The country's rand, already down 6 percent versus the dollar <ZAR=> since the start of the year, also eased 0.25 percent amid growing expectations of an early interest rate hike.\par \par \uc2 "BLUFFING" ATTEMPT\par \par \uc2 Selling pressure on emerging European \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  resumed a day after they bounced back on a coordinated push among the region's central bankers to talk up their \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 . [ID:nLI344803]\par \par \uc2 The unprecedented move saw the Czech and Polish central bankers join their Hungarian and Romanian counterparts to say that recent record falls in their \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  had been overdone.\par \par \uc2 But the sharp gains seen on Monday had mostly faded by Tuesday morning with few investors convinced that policymakers could back their words with actual \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 "We rather believe that it was a good attempt of bluffing as the central banks in central and eastern Europe most likely want to spare their reserves as much as possible due to coming outflows...While the \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  may have suffered "more than deserved" the key issue remains - very weak fundamentals and a struggling bank sector," said SEB in a client note.\par \par \uc2 Poland's zloty was down 0.77 percent against the euro <EURPLN=> while Romania's leu slipped 0.30 percent versus the common \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . <EURRON=>\par \par \uc2 Meanwhile, ratings agencies Fitch and \uc2 Moody's\uc2  issued fresh warnings on Latvia, Lithuania and Ukraine, warning of growing banking system and \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  risks from deteriorating macroeconomic conditions. [ID:nLO466428] [ID:nHKG366757] [nLO688554] [nLA378825]\par \par \uc2 Ukraine's \b \highlight22\uc2 hryvnia\b0 \highlight\uc2 , which fell nearly 7 percent on Monday, was quoted 3.7 percent weaker against the dollar. <UAH=>\par \par \uc2 Volumes remain thin with little dollars seen on offer in the market after the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  said it would not sell dollars to banks in its daily \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  if the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  traded at rates higher than its average rate.\par \par \uc2 Investors say the unit will remain pressured as long as Ukraine's deal with the International Monetary Fund (IMF) is stalled.\par \par \uc2 The IMF agreed to lend Ukraine $16.4 billion in a two-year plan of tranches and reforms promised by Kiev. But after pencilling in a three percent budget deficit this year -- contrary to IMF conditions -- the fund suspended the loan programme.\par \par \uc2 (Reporting by Sebastian Tong and Martina Fuchs; Editing by Victoria Main)\par \par \uc2 MARKETS-EMERGING|LANGEN|ABN|M|E|RBN|D|SF|RNP|DNP|PTD|PMF   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020090227e52o0013p\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
