\par\par \b \uc2 UPDATE 1-Ukraine cbank: IMF says initial conditions for loan met\b0\par\par\uc2 By Natalya Zinets   \par \uc2 363 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 28 Januar 2009\par 16:35\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2009 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 (Adds quotes, details)\par \par \uc2 KIEV, Jan 28 (Reuters) - A senior Ukrainian \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  official said on Wednesday the IMF had confirmed that initial conditions set for a $16.4 billion loan had been met.\par \par \uc2 An International Monetary Fund mission is in Kiev to assess progress on fiscal and monetary conditions it has set before disbursing the next tranche of the loan. Ukraine received $4.5 billion in November.\par \par \uc2 "The IMF has confirmed that all obligations which we undertook at the initial stages were fulfilled," the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's First Deputy Chairman, Anatoly Shapovalov, told a news conference.\par \par \uc2 The IMF required that foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves be no lower than $26.7 billion by the end of last year and the monetary base to be no higher than 190 billion dollars.\par \par \uc2 It also required the difference between the official rate, set by the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 , and the market rate to be no more than 2 percent.\par \par \uc2 That has not been the case for some of January when the official rate was 7.7/$, but the \b \highlight22\uc2 hryvnia\b0 \highlight\uc2  traded above 8.6/$. But Shapovalov said he hoped the IMF would accept the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's explanations that it was working to bring the rates closer.\par \par \uc2 "The \b \highlight22\uc2 hryvnia\b0 \highlight\uc2  depreciated 1.5-2 percent since the start of January. But we did not move the official rate in order not to create panic if only because after such a depreciation (in 2008) there is clearly no economic basis for it," he said.\par \par \uc2 He said the huge depreciation in the last four months of 2008, from 4.676 \b \highlight22\uc2 hryvnias\b0 \highlight\uc2  per dollar to historic lows touching upon 10/$, had helped the trade deficit in January.\par \par \uc2 He said exporters earned $2.339 billion, while payments for imports were at $2.008 billion. But pressure on the \b \highlight22\uc2 hryvnia\b0 \highlight\uc2  remained from foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  debt repayment and the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  intended to continue with \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  for now.\par \par \uc2 He said \b \highlight22\uc2 Ukraine\b0 \highlight\uc2  owed $1.6 billion in foreign debt in January and had paid up $1.536 billion.\par \par \uc2 (Editing by Ron Askew)\par \par \uc2 UKRAINE-CBANK/ (UPDATE 1)|LANGEN|ABN|M|D|BNX   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020090131e51s000db\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
