\par\par \b \uc2 Trade in Ukraine hrvynia drying up amid crisis\b0\par\par\uc2 By Peter Apps   \par \uc2 528 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 19 Dezember 2008\par 16:39\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2008 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 LONDON, Dec 19 (Reuters) - Trade in Ukraine's troubled hvrynia looked to be drying up on Friday with banks reporting no demand after the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  slumped in value and the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  tightened capital controls amid a deepening economic crisis.\par \par \uc2 After hitting historic lows in consecutive sessions, the \b \highlight22\uc2 hryvnia\b0 \highlight\uc2  recovered on Friday, supported by \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  auctions of dollars, a spike in the overnight refinancing rates and stability in the neighbouring Russian rouble.\par \par \uc2 The Reuters conversational dealing system quote for the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  in local trade <UAH=> showed the \b \highlight22\uc2 hryvnia\b0 \highlight\uc2  up 10.6 percent at 8.05 to the dollar but demand was almost non-existent.\par \par \uc2 At 1500 GMT, the system had not recorded any new prices since 1216 GMT -- although traders said occasional deals were being done.\par \par \uc2 The unit has lost roughly half its value to the dollar since June, much of it in the last few days when it fell to a record low beyond 9.5.\par \par \uc2 Liquidity in general across central and eastern European \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  has fallen sharply, with investors seeing the region as particularly exposed to the global financial crisis.\par \par \uc2 But after the collapse of Iceland, Ukraine is seen as the most likely next casualty despite an International Monetary Fund bailout.\par \par \uc2 Analysts say the plight of Ukraine -- suffering slumping steel prices, local banking problems and now a threatened cutting of Russian gas supply in the New Year -- is not as severe as Iceland, which had banking debts several times the size of its gross domestic product.\par \par \uc2 But the demise in trade in its \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  does bear some resemblance to the fate suffered by the Icelandic crown in September, when it likewise became practically impossible to exchange in international markets.\par \par \uc2 "It is not as bad as Iceland but it is close," said Lars Christensen, head of emerging markets research at \uc2 Danske Bank\uc2  in Copenhagen.\par \par \uc2 "No one wants to take any risks on the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . But overall the situation with liquidity across Central and Eastern Europe is very, very bad."\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Ukraine\b0 \highlight\uc2  had been \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  to hold its \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  higher but after haemorrhaging reserves and getting a $16.5 billion IMF deal, it has let the unit slide.\par \par \uc2 "The IMF plan called for a greater flexibility in the exchange rate and in a sense they are going back to that," said emerging markets \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategist Elizabeth Gruie at \uc2 BNP Paribas\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 International banks cannot trade the hrvynia except in the local market through local subsidiaries, and trade in the international non-deliverable forward (NDF) market -- in which they can trade -- looked to have dried up as well.\par \par \uc2 There were no forward trades from international banks showing on the Reuters system <UAHNDFOR=> on Friday.\par \par \uc2 "For the last three days, everyone has been looking for the right hand side (the sell side)," said a trader at a bank in London, adding that the occasional trade was going through but only driven by the needs of clients generally keen to ditch their positions.\par \par \uc2 (Additional reporting by Sebastian Tong and Carolyn Cohn; editing by Stephen Nisbet)\par \par \uc2 UKRAINE-\b \highlight22\uc2 CURRENCY\b0 \highlight\uc2 |LANGEN|C|D|E|M|O|U|MTL|GRO|SOF|OIL   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020081222e4cj00166\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
