\par\par \b \uc2 UPDATE:  \highlight22\uc2 Hryvnia \highlight\uc2  Hits New Low, Raises Credit Default Fears\b0\par\par\uc2 412 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 17 Dezember 2008\par 17:08\par \uc2 Dow Jones Emerging Markets Report\par \uc2 EM\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2008 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par    (Adds details, context, economist comments.) \par  \par    By Lidia Kelly \par    Of DOW JONES NEWSWIRES \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 MOSCOW (Dow Jones)--In what is becoming a daily occurrence, the Ukrainian \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 hryvnia\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  tumbled to a historic low Wednesday, raising fears of consumer credit default.\f28 \par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  weakened to UAH9.45 against the dollar as investors and the general public alike continued to desert the \b \highlight22\uc2 hryvnia\b0 \highlight\uc2  in favor of the dollar.\par \par \uc2 The slump came only two days after breaking through UAH8.0 and dragging the \b \highlight22\uc2 hryvnia\b0 \highlight\uc2 's purchasing power to barely half of what it was in the late summer.\par \par \uc2 The \uc2 National Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Ukraine\b0 \highlight\uc2  seems to have stepped back from \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  after buying some of the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  Tuesday, traders said.\par \par \uc2 Meanwhile, an economic aide to President Viktor Yushchenko, said the \b \highlight22\uc2 hryvnia\b0 \highlight\uc2 's current distressed level threatens consumer default.\par \par \uc2 "We can estimate that 60% of credits won't be paid back," Ukrainian news agencies cited the aide, Roman Zhukovsky, as saying.\par \par \uc2 The bank has been backed in its depreciation policy by a part of the $16.5 billion stabilization loan from the International Monetary Fund.\par \par \uc2 Last week, the head of the IMF's mission to Ukraine said the country has successfully absorbed a traumatic \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  devaluation.\par \par \uc2 Timothy Ash, head of Central and Eastern European research at \uc2 Royal Bank of Scotland Group PLC\uc2 , estimated that the National Bank still has some spare cash from the IMF loan to support the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , but warned that serious anti-crisis measures and reforms must be enforced.\par \par \uc2 "Having an IMF program isn't sufficient to ensuring an economy's passage through the current global crisis," Ash said in a research note.\par \par \uc2 New \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  data showed the country's external debt increased by $7.4 billion in the third quarter to $105.4 billion, or 60% of gross domestic product, with short-term liabilities estimated at $30 billion.\par \par \uc2 The news, compounded by a widening current account deficit, further political wrangling about anti-crisis policy and uncertainty over the new coalition between the parties of Yushchenko and Prime Minister Yulia Tymoshenko, only adds to the \b \highlight22\uc2 hryvnia\b0 \highlight\uc2 's woes, economists said.\par \par \uc2 "In Ukraine, the evidence is still that policymakers don't quite understand the seriousness of the challenges they face," Ash said.\par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par    National Bank Web site: \f28 {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "http://www.bank.gov.ua"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 www.bank.gov.ua}}}\par \par \uc2 \f2 -By Lidia Kelly, Dow Jones Newswires; +7 495 937 8445; lidia.kelly@dowjones.com\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 (Clare Connaghan in London contributed to this report). [ 17-12-08 1608GMT ]\f28 \par \par \uc2 Dokument EM00000020081217e4ch00019\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
