\par\par \b \uc2 UDPATE 1- \highlight22\uc2 Ukraine \highlight\uc2 's cbank returns to  \highlight22\uc2 intervention \highlight\b0\par\par\uc2 365 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 21 November 2008\par 14:42\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2008 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 (Adds cbank official, details)\par \par \uc2 KIEV, Nov 21 (Reuters) - \b \highlight22\uc2 Ukraine\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  sold dollars on the interbank market on Friday in its weeks-long effort to support the \b \highlight22\uc2 hryvnia\b0 \highlight\uc2  and said it would continue with \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  and auctions to find the best way to shore up the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 The bank has been spending billions of dollars in \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  throughout most of October and November. The \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  fell to a historic low in mid-October of 7.05-7.2 per dollar.\par \par \uc2 The bank on Wednesday conducted an auction for the dollar in what had been seen as a policy shift. It failed to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  on Thursday and the \b \highlight22\uc2 hryvnia\b0 \highlight\uc2  slipped to 6.5 to the dollar from 6.2 the previous day.\par \par \uc2 The bank sold dollars at 6.17 \b \highlight22\uc2 hryvnias\b0 \highlight\uc2  on Friday and the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  strengthened to 6.00-6.24.\par \par \uc2 "For now we will carry out both auctions and \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2 ," a \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  official said. "We need time to sharpen our auctioning method so that the process is transparent and to understand which way is the most effective."\par \par \uc2 The official said the volume of dollar sales on Friday was not high. The bank spent $4.115 billion on \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in October, according to its own data. Dealers have said that it has spent about $3 billion so far in November.\par \par \uc2 Ukraine has agreed a loan from the International Monetary Fund, some of which may go towards propping up reserves though the fund in general prefers greater \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  flexibility.\par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  fell in the past two months at first because investors sold their Ukrainian assets and bought dollars, fleeing risky emerging markets in the face of the global financial crisis.\par \par \uc2 Ukraine's exports have fallen dramatically as economies slow down, especially hurting steelmakers who account for 45 percent of exports -- which means they have far fewer dollars to trade.\par \par \uc2 A fast-expanding current account gap and an expected slowdown in foreign direct investment next year both point to a weaker \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . (Reporting by Natalya Zinets; writing by Sabina Zawadzki; Editing by Ruth Pitchford)\par \par \uc2 UKRAINE-CBANK (UPDATE 1)|LANGEN|ABN|M|E|RBN|D|RNP   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020081121e4bl001lk\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
