\par\par \b \uc2 UPDATE 2-Ukraine c.bank starts dollar sale auction\b0\par\par\uc2 By Natalya Zinets   \par \uc2 501 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 19 November 2008\par 11:32\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2008 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 (adds C.Bank selling dollars at auction at 5.98)\par \par \uc2 KIEV, Nov 19 (Reuters) - In a major policy shift, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  abandoned direct \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  to support \b \highlight22\uc2 Ukraine\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 hryvnia currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  on Wednesday and sold dollars for the first time at an auction to banks offering 5.98 or more per dollar.\par \par \uc2 Dealers said all transactions occurred at 5.98, though that did not become clear until after 5 p.m. when trading closed.\par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  had been \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  virtually every day on the interbank market since early October, but took no such action on Tuesday, allowing the \b \highlight22\uc2 hryvnia\b0 \highlight\uc2  to slip to 6.0 to the dollar from 5.83 the previous day.\par \par \uc2 "They covered our bid at 5.98 though we had put our bid even higher so as to take no risks," said one dealer. "We had quite a significant volume."\par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  gave no explanation for introducing the auctions.\par \par \uc2 "Perhaps they are hoping to reduce demand for purchases (of dollars)," said one dealer, recalling that Ukrainian authorities had promised the IMF to spend less of its reserves on \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  and pursue a flexible exchange rate policy.\par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 hryvnia\b0 \highlight\uc2  fell further on the interbank market to 6.10-6.15 to the dollar, and not all participants were happy with the new system.\par \par \uc2 "The rate is determined under this system not by supply and demand, but through \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  and it is impossible to determine in advance whether this will happen," said one dealer. The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  had earlier issued a directive allowing banks to buy dollars at 5.8854 \b \highlight22\uc2 hryvnias\b0 \highlight\uc2  plus or minus two percent.\par \par \uc2 It said banks could buy dollars according to the rate proposed, with higher rates for the dollar first, until a fixed sum of \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  funds was exhausted. It identified no sum.\par \par \uc2 Banks need not identify the reason for buying, it said, but had to specify a rate "to within two places after the decimal point" and a volume, with a minimum purchase of $100,000.\par \par \uc2 Banks were required to submit bids by 2 p.m. (1200 GMT).\par \par \uc2 In a memorandum signed with the International Monetary Fund this month to underpin a $16.4 billion loan, Ukrainian authorities undertook to narrow differences between official, interbank, cash and \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  rates for the \b \highlight22\uc2 hryvnia\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 They pledged to keep to no more than two percent the gap between the market and official rates.\par \par \uc2 The bank altered its \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  tactics after the \b \highlight22\uc2 hryvnia\b0 \highlight\uc2  sank to a historic low of below 7.0 to the dollar last month by purchasing dollars on the interbank market without limit.\par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 hryvnia\b0 \highlight\uc2  regained ground to a rate stronger than 6.0 but the \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  failed to curb excess demand for dollars resulting from foreign capital moving out of Ukraine and declining markets for Ukrainian exports. (Reporting by Natalya Zinets, writing by Ron Popeski; Editing by Ruth Pitchford)\par \par \uc2 UKRAINE-CBANK/ (UPDATE 2)|LANGEN|ABN|M|D|BNX   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020081119e4bj000us\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
