\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 Ukraine hryvnia \highlight\uc2  slips with no c.Bank  \highlight22\uc2 intervention \highlight\b0\par\par\uc2 By Natalya Zinets   \par \uc2 558 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 18 November 2008\par 17:27\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2008 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 KIEV, Nov 18 (Reuters) - \b \highlight22\uc2 Ukraine\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 hryvnia\b0 \highlight\uc2  slipped to 6.0 to the dollar on Tuesday from 5.83 the previous day in the absence of what in recent weeks has become routine \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  to support the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  on Monday, selling dollars on the interbank market at 5.79.\par \par \uc2 "In the absence of the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 , trading slipped below 5.90, but I can't say there is any panic," said one dealer.\par \par \uc2 "But we could fall to 7.0 tomorrow. There were offers to buy dollars at 6.10. There were some deals this morning at 5.97 but the amounts were very small."\par \par \uc2 Traders said the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  had given no explanation for not supporting the \b \highlight22\uc2 hryvnia\b0 \highlight\uc2  as it has for nearly two months.\par \par \uc2 "People are saying it's because of the IMF, that the Fund is unhappy, that this is not a real market and that reserves are being spent -- and not on structural changes," said one dealer.\par \par \uc2 The International Monetary Fund this month agreed to give Ukraine a $16.4 billion loan to stabilise the economy and the banking system and has disbursed the first $4.5 billion tranche.\par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  in October spent $4.115 \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  on the market to sell dollars. It had in recent weeks pledged to sell dollars without limit.\par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's deputy chairman, Oleskander Savchenko, told a weekly newspaper on Monday that the \b \highlight22\uc2 hryvnia\b0 \highlight\uc2  would remain stable at 5.5-6.0 and strengthen in the second half of 2009. He ruled out as improbable any decline to weaker than 7.0.\par \par \uc2 But Oleskander Shlapak, top economic adviser to Ukraine's president, renewed the criticism he had directed at the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  in October, when the \b \highlight22\uc2 hryvnia\b0 \highlight\uc2  sank to 7.0. He said he was again unhappy with developments on the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market.\par \par \uc2 "Things are not well on the market," he told a briefing. I'm talking about the level of demand (for dollars) over five or six days -- about $1 billion every day. That raises many questions."\par \par \uc2 Levels of imports and purchases of dollars by consumers did not justify that level, he said, and President Viktor Yushchenko would seek explanations at a meeting on Thursday with bankers.\par \par \uc2 "If this is psychological and speculative demand, we know how to deal with it," he said. "If we do not have a balanced rate, then measures must be taken to set down such a trend."\par \par \uc2 Dealers said the thrust of official policy was hard to gauge given the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  chairman's pledge that the \b \highlight22\uc2 hryvnia\b0 \highlight\uc2  would go no weaker than 6.0 and that there would no longer be any discrepancies between the market rate and an "official" rate.\par \par \uc2 "You have to be consistent. They said there would be a single rate. They said they would sell dollars without limit. Where is the single rate?" said one dealer.\par \par \uc2 "And the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  is saying nothing. You cannot restore confidence with inconsistent moves. Dealers and the public will rely only on themselves. Why not buy a dollar today at 6.20, if it will cost 7.0 tomorrow?" (Additional reporting by Yuri Kulikov, writing by Ron Popeski; Editing by Ron Askew)\par \par \uc2 UKRAINE-\b \highlight22\uc2 CURRENCY\b0 \highlight\uc2 /|LANGEN|ABN|M|D|BNX   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020081118e4bi0019r\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
