\par\par \b \uc2 Ukraine president's office slams cbank on  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2  policy\b0\par\par\uc2 150 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 30 Oktober 2008\par 10:49\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2008 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 KIEV, Oct 30 (Reuters) - The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has failed to stabilise the \b \highlight22\uc2 hryvnia currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  despite selling almost $5 billion in three weeks and must introduce a transparent mechanism for \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , an aide to \b \highlight22\uc2 Ukraine\b0 \highlight\uc2 's president said on Thursday.\par \par \uc2 "Over three weeks (the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 ) has spent nearly $5 billion dollars of the country's reserves, but the market has felt no positive effect of this colossal \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 ," Oleksander Shlapak, a top economic aide to President Viktor Yushchenko, said on the presidential Web site.\par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  has been falling against the dollar for several weeks and lost almost 15 percent of its value on Wednesday. On Thursday, it bounced from historic lows and traded at 6.2-6.5 to the dollar.\par \par \uc2 (Editing by Patrick Graham)\par \par \uc2 UKRAINE-CBANK/ (URGENT)|LANGEN|ABN|M|E|RBN|D|G|RNP|PGE   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020081030e4au0018e\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
