\par\par \b \uc2 UPDATE 2-Ukraine parliament fails to act on IMF credit\b0\par\par\uc2 512 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 28 Oktober 2008\par 09:28\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2008 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 (New story; parliament fails to act)\par \par \uc2 KIEV, Oct 28 (Reuters) - Ukraine's parliament, mired in a long-running political row over a snap election, failed again on Tuesday to consider legislation needed to secure an IMF bailout programme of credits worth $16.5 billion.\par \par \uc2 Supporters of Prime Minister Yulia Tymoshenko, who opposes the election, charged up to the chairman's rostrum to prevent what they suspected would be a move to put election finance on the agenda alongside the IMF legislation.\par \par \uc2 Chairman Arseniy Yatsenyuk acknowledged deadlock over the agenda. He scolded deputies for blocking debate -- and approval of the International Monetary Fund credit officials say is needed to stabilise Ukraine's financial and banking systems.\par \par \uc2 "Everything came down to what was supposed to be examined first -- measures to tackle the crisis or a bill on holding an early election. And that's where matters have ended," he said.\par \par \uc2 "I understand that adopting the package of measures will not save us from everything ... We cannot subdue the economic and political crisis entirely. But let's set down as a priority the economic and political baselines."\par \par \uc2 Parliament, the chairman said, would be called into session on Wednesday to approve the measures in a first reading. Parties would then submit proposals for a second and final reading.\par \par \uc2 Yatsenyuk had asked deputies to consider a compromise package to satisfy what are believed to be IMF demands for the credit. Analysts say these include a balanced 2009 budget, greater \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  flexibility and banking sector reforms.\par \par \uc2 The IMF and the government announced preliminary agreement on the loan package at the weekend. The Fund has made no comment on what conditions it has set and it was unclear whether the package under consideration met the demands.\par \par \uc2 Markets remained unimpressed by the agreement. The \b \highlight22\uc2 hryvnia currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  traded at 6.3-6.4 to the dollar, close to its all-time low, despite daily \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Ukraine\b0 \highlight\uc2  was pitched into its latest bout of political upheaval by President Viktor Yushchenko's dissolution of parliament last month and call for a December election, which would be the third in as many years in the ex-Soviet state.\par \par \uc2 Both Tymoshenko and Yushchenko, allies from the pro-Western 2004 "Orange Revolution" now turned rivals, want quick adoption of the anti-crisis measures to secure IMF help.\par \par \uc2 A government statement said Tymoshenko and IMF Managing Director Dominique Strauss-Kahn had spoken by telephone, urged parliament to act promptly and called for political stability.\par \par \uc2 But Tymoshenko says an election would be "criminal" amid the world crisis. Her allies vow to disrupt debate until they get assurances no move will be made to finance the contest.\par \par \uc2 Yushchenko blames the premier for the collapse of the latest governing "orange coalition" and says only an election can solve the impasse. (Writing by Ron Popeski; Editing by Giles Elgood)\par \par \uc2 UKRAINE-IMF/ (UPDATE 2, PIX)|LANGEN|AFA|CSA|LBY|RWSA|RWS|REULB|GNS|G|RBN|C|D|E|M|O|U|MTL|GRO|SOF|OIL|RNP|PGE   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020081028e4as000p8\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
