\par\par \b \uc2 WRAPUP 1-Ukraine PM risks losing IMF credit: president's aide\b0\par\par\uc2 866 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 27 Oktober 2008\par 18:35\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2008 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 * Presidential aide criticises PM\par \par \uc2 * \b \highlight22\uc2 Hryvnia\b0 \highlight\uc2  hits record low, stock dive 4 pct\par \par \uc2 * Fitch sees threat to Ukraine rating\par \par \uc2 By Ron Popeski\par \par \uc2 KIEV, Oct 27 (Reuters) - An aide to Ukraine's president accused Prime Minister Yulia Tymoshenko on Monday of putting a big IMF credit at risk by linking quick approval of financial legislation with the country's long-running political upheaval.\par \par \uc2 The International Monetary Fund and Ukraine agreed on Sunday on a $16.5 billion credit for the ex-Soviet state, subject to approval of financial measures by the fractious parliament, which was blockaded last week by the prime minister's allies.\par \par \uc2 Tymoshenko and her supporters last week blocked discussion of the financial package for four days in order to prevent inclusion in it of any funding for disputed early elections, called by Yushchenko for next month.\par \par \uc2 Markets were unimpressed by news of the credit. The \b \highlight22\uc2 hryvnia currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  sank to a record low, prompting the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  to abandon a corridor to control its movements.\par \par \uc2 The tiny stock market plunged a further four percent and credit default swaps, an indication of risk that Ukraine could default on debts, rose to 2,600 basis points from 300 in August.\par \par \uc2 Ratings agency Fitch said further tumbles in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  could put Ukraine's rating under pressure, but acknowledged that the IMF accord could help restore confidence.\par \par \uc2 Parliamentary approval of financial legislation is critical to the deal. The chamber is due to consider the legislation on Tuesday after a weekend of talks to produce a compromise package to ease the effects of the world financial crisis.\par \par \uc2 But Ukraine also remains gripped by political turbulence sparked by President Viktor Yushchenko's dissolution of parliament and call for a new election.\par \par \uc2 Presidential aide Andriy Goncharuk said the prime minister was acting against the national interest by lobbying at the same time for the cancellation of the December election.\par \par \uc2 "It is a pity that the position of the prime minister's office reduces the chances for the country to receive the first tranche of the credit awaited so long by the financial system," Goncharuk said in a statement on the president's Web site.\par \par \uc2 "An election must be seen as the sole way to resolve the political crisis, not a catalyst for economic problems. The lack of a viable parliament is a much greater risk for the country than a quick campaign and formation of a stable majority."\par \par \uc2 Yushchenko, long at odds with Tymoshenko, called the election after the collapse last month of a coalition of groups led by him and the prime minister.\par \par \uc2 "CRIMINAL" ELECTION\par \par \uc2 Tymoshenko says an election would be "criminal" in the current financial crisis and her backers last week prevented any discussion in parliament of funding for the poll.\par \par \uc2 With no let up in political turmoil, the \b \highlight22\uc2 hryvnia currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  slumped to a record low of 6.2 to the dollar despite the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's now routine \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  council chief Petro Poroshenko announced the elimination of a newly-widened 4.554-5.346 corridor. He said \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  had sapped 10 percent of reserves and indicated \b \highlight22\uc2 Ukraine\b0 \highlight\uc2  would seek a further $3 billion in international loans.\par \par \uc2 Analysts have expressed concerned over the ability of the government, firms and banks to refinance.\par \par \uc2 The head of the IMF mission which has been in Kiev for more than a week praised authorities' resolve, while making no reference to conditions attached to the loan.\par \par \uc2 "I must say that they (the government and \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 ) are being extremely proactive, they have been working on policies in parliament," Ceyla Pazarbasioglu told top officials.\par \par \uc2 Analysts believe the Fund wants a balanced budget, greater flexibility on \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets and banking sector reforms.\par \par \uc2 Tymoshenko said she hoped the chamber would come to a consensus and approve the "anti-crisis package" without delay.\par \par \uc2 "We fully believe that tomorrow, Tuesday, a package of legislative measures to combat the crisis must be adopted in parliament," she told reporters.\par \par \uc2 Yushchenko, speaking during a visit to Turkey, also hoped parliament would act quickly on the package.\par \par \uc2 Parliament's chairman, Arseniy Yatsenyuk, last week said failure to pass the measures could imperil talks with the IMF.\par \par \uc2 On Monday, he said discussions were proceeding to narrow differences and produce a compromise document.\par \par \uc2 "There is so far no agreement on a bill and we aren't going to get one," he said.\par \par \uc2 "My experts are meeting those from different groups to put together the shortest possible document from the 40 pages proposed by the government in order to increase the likelihood of it being approved."\par \par \uc2 Oleksander Okhrymenko, senior adviser to Ukrgazbank, said the IMF deal might reduce some panic, but he remained sceptical.\par \par \uc2 "Those who follow the politics and parliament clearly believe that we will never receive the money because it is most unlikely the laws will be adopted," he said. (Additional reporting by Natalya Zinets, Sabina Zawadzki, Yuri Kulikov and by Zerin Elci in Ankara; Editing by Jon Boyle)\par \par \uc2 FINANCIAL-UKRAINE/ (WRAPUP 1, TV)|LANGEN|AFA|CSA|LBY|RWSA|RWS|REULB|GNS|ABX|BNX|FUN|G|RBN|C|D|E|M|O|U|MTL|GRO|SOF|OIL|RNP|PGE   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020081027e4ar001w8\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
