\par\par \b \uc2 UPDATE 2-Ukraine's  \highlight22\uc2 hryvnia \highlight\uc2 , stocks drop, CDS rocket\b0\par\par\uc2 By Sabina Zawadzki   \par \uc2 599 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 7 Oktober 2008\par 17:12\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2008 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 (Adds cbank deputy head, analysts, more CDS, yields)\par \par \uc2 KIEV, Oct 7 (Reuters) - \b \highlight22\uc2 Ukraine\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  said it would \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  to strengthen the \b \highlight22\uc2 hryvnia\b0 \highlight\uc2  to about 5.0 to the dollar after the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  sank on Tuesday to lows that weaker than those set during the 2004 "Orange Revolution".\par \par \uc2 Banking shares were hit on the PFTS exchange, which closed 8 percent down and almost 50 percent lower than Sept. 1, and the cost of insuring against a Ukrainian sovereign default rocketed as investors continued to flee emerging markets.\par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 hryvnia\b0 \highlight\uc2  traded at 5.54-5.60 to the dollar, its lowest since February 2004. The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  made no offer to sell dollars, according to Reuters data.\par \par \uc2 But that was about to change, Oleksander Savchenko, the deputy chairman of the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 , said.\par \par \uc2 "We will support the \b \highlight22\uc2 hryvnia\b0 \highlight\uc2  though \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 . We will \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  considerably and the \b \highlight22\uc2 hryvnia\b0 \highlight\uc2  will return to its old level rather quickly," Savchenko told Fifth Channel television. He referred to 5.0 to the dollar as a favourable level.\par \par \uc2 The bank's council also widened its forecast band for the \b \highlight22\uc2 hryvnia\b0 \highlight\uc2  for this year to 4.95 per dollar plus or minus 8 percent from 4.85 plus or minus 4 percent, bringing the band to 4.554-5.346.\par \par \uc2 "The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  should keep to this band and has to start \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  tomorrow morning. The best it can do is to calm the market while they can," \uc2 Unicredit\uc2  analyst Dmitry Gourov said.\par \par \uc2 Savchenko's comments appeared to mark a change of heart at the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Its officials, including Savchenko, had indicated it would not \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  regularly to avoid boosting the current account gap and because the \b \highlight22\uc2 hryvnia\b0 \highlight\uc2  was being battered by temporary factors.\par \par \uc2 Fitch cut Ukraine's outlook last month, warning of a higher risk of a \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  crisis given the gaping current account deficit.\par \par \uc2 The bank has been building up record foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves, but at just under $38 billion, some wonder whether that would be enough to shore up the \b \highlight22\uc2 hryvnia\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 "What we do know is that the reserve coverage is below the bank's comfort zone with respect to imports. We don't know what tolerance they have," said Citi economist Ali Al-Eyd.\par \par \uc2 RECORD BROKEN\par \par \uc2 The cost of insuring against default or restructuring rose to record levels at 850-1,000 basis points, brokers said, meaning investors were quoted between $850,000 to $1 million a year for five years to insure against $10 million of debt.\par \par \uc2 CDS on Naftogaz, Ukraine's ailing state energy firm, were even higher at 1,700 basis points.\par \par \uc2 Investors typically become more cautious, demanding upfront payments in addition to annual payments, when credit default swaps reach around 1,000 bps.\par \par \uc2 Brokers started quoting Iceland's CDS on an upfront basis last week, shortly before the country went to Russia for a bail-out package for its banks.\par \par \uc2 Ukrainian yields, meanwhile, widened 133 basis points to 12.18 percent above U.S. treasury yields. The stock market closed 8.15 percent down at 319.67 points, bringing the loss since Sept. 1, when investors lost appetite for the region, to 47 percent. It suspended trading in seven companies, then in the whole index altogether for several hours.\par \par \uc2 Unicredit\uc2 's unit \uc2 Ukrsotsbank\uc2  lost 24 percent and Raiffeisen's \uc2 Bank Aval\uc2  lost 23 percent. (Additional reporting by Natalya Zinets in Kiev and Carolyn Cohn in London, editing by Swaha Pattanaik)\par \par \uc2 UKRAINE-\b \highlight22\uc2 CURRENCY\b0 \highlight\uc2  (UPDATE 2)|LANGEN|ABN|M|E|RBN|D|BNX|RNP   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020081007e4a7001c8\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
