\par\par \b \uc2 Romania cbank may prop up leu near 4 per euro-analysts\b0\par\par\uc2 By Luiza Ilie and Marius Zaharia   \par \uc2 535 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 6 Oktober 2008\par 10:00\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2008 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 BUCHAREST, Oct 6 (Reuters) - Romania's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  (BNR) could \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  this week to support the leu and shore up its inflation targets after the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  sank around 10 percent over the last month to an almost four-year low, analysts said on Monday.\par \par \uc2 With the leu bid at weaker than 3.9 per euro -- nudging a four-year low -- analysts have increasingly alluded to testing a "BNR put", in which they believe the bank will feel obliged to prop up the leu <EURRON=> at around 4.0 or 4.1 per euro.\par \par \uc2 It would be necessary, they say, to prevent a possible banking crisis. Because 55 percent of Romanian loans are in foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 , firms and households could have trouble paying back loans if the leu slides more against the euro.\par \par \uc2 "The BNR has a lot to lose if EUR/RON rises substantially above the psychological level of 4.00. Therefore, the bank is likely step into the market, potentially already (this) week," said \uc2 JP Morgan\uc2  analyst Miroslav Plojhar.\par \par \uc2 Emerging European \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  have been pummelled as investors avoid risk and hoard cash following the downfall of major financial institutions, but none more than the leu.\par \par \uc2 On Monday morning, it shed 1.8 percent to 3.944 against the euro, following heavy losses at the end of last week.\par \par \uc2 Romania's more developed ex-communist peers -- Poland, the Czech Republic and Hungary -- have seen their \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  slip 3.4 to 4.5 percent since Sept. 12 when U.S. bank \uc2 Lehman Brothers\uc2  filed for bankruptcy, but analysts said their banks would keep to the sidelines because they were still relatively strong.\par \par \uc2 For Romania, the financial crisis has heightened concerns, voiced by rating agencies and the International Monetary Fund, that the country is more vulnerable than its peers because of a vast current account deficit, high rates of hard \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  borrowing and inadequate fiscal and wage policies.\par \par \uc2 The fear is the Romanian economy could be destabilised if global cash flows and foreign investment dry up and are no longer sufficient to plug the double-digit external deficit.\par \par \uc2 "They should \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  to stop the depreciation because otherwise this will have a major impact on inflation and will throw inflationary expectations in the air," said Ionut Dumitru, head of research at Raiffeisen Bank in Bucharest.\par \par \uc2 Inflation is expected to fall to around 6 percent in December, still above the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's 2.8-4.8 percent target.\par \par \uc2 The bank kept its benchmark rate on hold at 10.25 percent at its last meeting in September, but analysts said another hike may be on the cards due to pledges by major parties to loosen fiscal policy ahead of a Nov. 30 parliamentary election.\par \par \uc2 Elsewhere in the region, Serbia's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  to tame dinar losses after \b \highlight22\uc2 Ukraine\b0 \highlight\uc2  stepped in to buy local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  at 5 \b \highlight22\uc2 hryvnias\b0 \highlight\uc2  to the dollar <UAH=> on Friday.\par \par \uc2 "We've seen \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  in \b \highlight22\uc2 Ukraine\b0 \highlight\uc2 , Serbia. The next to come is Romania," said Elisabeth Gruie, \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategist at \uc2 BNP Paribas\uc2 . (Editing by Victoria Main)\par \par \uc2 ROMANIA-LEU/\b \highlight22\uc2 INTERVENTION\b0 \highlight\uc2 |LANGEN|ABN|M|D|RDN|GNN|DNP   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020081006e4a6000jd\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
