\par\par \b \uc2 UPDATE 1-Ukraine cbank offers dollars at 5.0  \highlight22\uc2 hryvnias \highlight\b0\par\par\uc2 278 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 3 Oktober 2008\par 10:21\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2008 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 (Adds background, new \b \highlight22\uc2 hryvnia\b0 \highlight\uc2  rate)\par \par \uc2 KIEV, Oct 3 (Reuters) - Ukraine's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  offered dollars at 5.0 \b \highlight22\uc2 hryvnias\b0 \highlight\uc2  on Friday, according to Reuters data that showed the bank's first \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  to support the \b \highlight22\uc2 hryvnia\b0 \highlight\uc2  since February.\par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has let the \b \highlight22\uc2 hryvnia\b0 \highlight\uc2  fluctuate much more freely since February, abandoning a three-year policy of keeping it within a strict corridor 5.00-5.06 to the dollar. The \b \highlight22\uc2 hryvnia\b0 \highlight\uc2  strengthened to as much as 4.5 per dollar throughout May and June.\par \par \uc2 But in recent weeks the \b \highlight22\uc2 hryvnia\b0 \highlight\uc2  has lost all of those gains, hitting a 3-1/2-year low of 5.11-5.12 on Wednesday.\par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 hryvnia\b0 \highlight\uc2  had been trading at 5.18-5.26 per dollar earlier in the morning before the bank made the offer. It strengthened within minutes of the offer to 5.053-5.19.\par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's deputy chairman, Oleksander Savchenko, said on Thursday the bank would not prop up the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  for now because much of the weakness was temporary and any such move could deepen the current account gap.\par \par \uc2 The bank on Thursday released a statement to say it would not spend its reserves when speculators were in the market, but could \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  to help with purchases of crucial imports and payments for external debt.\par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  was not immediately available for comment after Friday's move.\par \par \uc2 Some analysts have warned against the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  letting the \b \highlight22\uc2 hryvnia\b0 \highlight\uc2  fluctuate too much because it risked "losing the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  as a nominal anchor".\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 UKRAINE\b0 \highlight\uc2 -\b \highlight22\uc2 CURRENCY\b0 \highlight\uc2 /\b \highlight22\uc2 INTERVENTION\b0 \highlight\uc2  (UPDATE 1)|LANGEN|ABN|M|D   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020081006e4a3000ku\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
