\par\par \b \uc2 UPDATE 2-Ukraine C.Bank buys dollars at 4.75  \highlight22\uc2 hryvnias \highlight\b0\par\par\uc2 328 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 15 Juli 2008\par 11:50\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2008 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 (Adds new official \b \highlight22\uc2 hryvnia\b0 \highlight\uc2  rate)\par \par \uc2 KIEV, July 15 (Reuters) - \b \highlight22\uc2 Ukraine\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  on the interbank market on Tuesday, buying dollars at 4.75 \b \highlight22\uc2 hryvnias\b0 \highlight\uc2  after announcing it would bid at that level, dealers said.\par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  last \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  on July 10, buying dollars at 4.74.\par \par \uc2 "The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  came on the market, but bought only in a moderate fashion -- only a part of clients' bids -- 20-30 percent of bank limits," said one dealer.\par \par \uc2 Dealers said transactions initially took place at 4.6-4.61 to the dollar, but after the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  indicated its readiness to bid, the \b \highlight22\uc2 hryvnia\b0 \highlight\uc2  fell back to 4.65-4.67.\par \par \uc2 The bank also announced its latest adjustment to the official \b \highlight22\uc2 hryvnia\b0 \highlight\uc2  rate, setting it at 4.8401 from Wednesday, July 16. The previous rate, valid from Tuesday, was 4.8413.\par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  abandoned a three-year-old policy of keeping the \b \highlight22\uc2 hryvnia\b0 \highlight\uc2  within a corridor of 5.0-5.06 around February-March and in May revalued the official rate to 4.85 from 5.05. It now adjusts that rate periodically.\par \par \uc2 Some market participants said a number of clients were willing to sell dollars only to the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  at the highest possible rate, but sometimes had to wait to process transactions as the bank did not \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  every day.\par \par \uc2 Dollar supply, in any event, was starting to decline, they said.\par \par \uc2 "Dollar supply always starts to go down as summer wears on," said one dealer. "You can feel that we are at a specific point on this now. People understand the market won't go below 4.6."\par \par \uc2 Last week, a senior \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  official said bank purchases of dollars had pushed reserves up to $36 billion, including $1 billion in the first 10 days of July. (Reporting by Natalya Zinets)\par \par \uc2 UKRAINE-\b \highlight22\uc2 CURRENCY\b0 \highlight\uc2 /BID (UPDATE 2)|LANGEN|ABN|M|D|BNX   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020080715e47f000wl\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
