\par\par \b \uc2 UPDATE 1- \highlight22\uc2 Ukraine \highlight\uc2  C.Bank  \highlight22\uc2 intervenes \highlight\uc2 , alters official  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2  rate\b0\par\par\uc2 By Natalya Zinets   \par \uc2 572 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 29 Mai 2008\par 10:33\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2008 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 (adds new official rate, details)\par \par \uc2 KIEV, May 29 (Reuters) - Ukraine's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  on Thursday altered the \b \highlight22\uc2 hryvnia currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 's official rate, proceeding with a new policy of flexibility on the market after three years of defending a set rate.\par \par \uc2 In an announcement on its Internet site {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "http://www.bank.gov.ua"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 www.bank.gov.ua}}}\uc2 , the bank said the official rate of 4.852 \b \highlight22\uc2 hryvnias\b0 \highlight\uc2  to the dollar would take effect from Friday, against the previous rate of 4.85 which had applied since the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  was revalued on May 22.\par \par \uc2 The announcement came after the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  on the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market on Thursday, buying dollars at 4.84 \b \highlight22\uc2 hryvnias\b0 \highlight\uc2 , compared with 4.80 at which it stepped into the market on May 23.\par \par \uc2 "The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  is proceeding with transactions, but the dollar rose immediately after it indicated its readiness to buy," one dealer said.\par \par \uc2 "The dollar was trading yesterday and this morning at 4.715/4.73 and now it is about 4.8 and higher."\par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  had maintained the \b \highlight22\uc2 hryvnia\b0 \highlight\uc2  in a corridor of 5.0-5.06 until recent months, but revalued the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  on May 22 at 4.8 and began buying dollars at that level last week for the first time since September 2007.\par \par \uc2 The dollar had fallen on the interbank market to between 4.5 and 4.6 \b \highlight22\uc2 hryvnias\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the days preceding the revaluation.\par \par \uc2 The bank's top adviser, Valery Lytvytsky, said last week the revaluation was an indication the bank now wanted to introduce a measure of flexibility on the interbank market.\par \par \uc2 COMPROMISE\par \par \uc2 Dealers believed the higher bid indicated the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's board was seeking a compromise with its policy-making council, which had vetoed the revaluation and called for a return to the previous official rate of 5.05.\par \par \uc2 Council head Petro Poroshenko said the board first had to agree with its members on new limits within a long-established broader corridor of 4.95-5.25 to the dollar before proceeding with a revaluation.\par \par \uc2 But the board overturned the council's veto, with \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  chief Volodymyr Stelmakh saying market realities prompted the board to go forward with the revaluation.\par \par \uc2 Ukraine's parliament summoned both Stelmakh and Poroshenko for an explanation of \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  policy and urged the board and council to find a compromise.\par \par \uc2 "I believe the two sides have started to work out an agreement and find an acceptable rate," said one dealer. "I would not be surprised to see the dollar rate climb next week depending on what sort of corridor is agreed."\par \par \uc2 Poroshenko said on Monday new guidelines for a corridor would be worked out within two weeks.\par \par \uc2 Stelmakh is scheduled to hold a news conference on Friday.\par \par \uc2 Analysts said they expected the high end of the corridor to be raised beyond 4.95, while the lower end of 5.25 is seen kept intact.\par \par \uc2 An anticipated worsening of the nation's trade balance and expected new rises in the price of gas imports made any further rise in the \b \highlight22\uc2 hryvnia\b0 \highlight\uc2 's value unlikely, analysts said.\par \par \uc2 "The historical trend in Ukraine is clear -- large purchases of dollars in the autumn by importers," said one dealer. "We believe demand for the dollar will be high." (Writing by Ron Popeski; Editing by Leika Kihara)\par \par \uc2 UKRAINE/CBANK (UPDATE 1)|LANGEN|ABN|M|D|BNX   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020080529e45t000ks\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
