\par\par \b \uc2 UPDATE 1- \highlight22\uc2 Ukraine \highlight\uc2  cenbank  \highlight22\uc2 intervenes \highlight\uc2 , sells dollars   \b0\par\par\uc2 269 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 31 Januar 2008\par 15:53\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2008 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 (Adds comment, background)   \par \par \uc2 KIEV, Jan 31 (Reuters) - The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  resumed its \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  on \b \highlight22\uc2 Ukraine\b0 \highlight\uc2 's interbank market on Thursday, selling dollars at 5.06 \b \highlight22\uc2 hryvnias\b0 \highlight\uc2  to keep the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  within a long-standing narrow corridor, dealers said.   \par \par \uc2 "Had the bank seen a sufficient level of supply of foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , it would have stayed out of the market," said one dealer. "But clearly the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  had a good look at bank orders and saw there was insufficient supply."   \par \par \uc2 The bank had \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  for six days in a row up until Tuesday, but stayed out of the market on Wednesday. It has kept the \b \highlight22\uc2 hryvnia currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  at 5.00-5.06 to the dollar since August 2005.   \par \par \uc2 Dealers reported few sharp movements in transactions on Thursday, though the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  shifted downward to the level of \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  soon after the market opened.   \par \par \uc2 "There is a clear reason for higher demand for dollars at the end of the month as people have to make payments for imports and credits," said one dealer. The bank has bought or sold dollars as required to keep the \b \highlight22\uc2 hryvnia\b0 \highlight\uc2  within the prescribed limits -- buying practically throughout 2007, with the exception of sales in December.   \par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's executive director on economic issues, Ihor Shumylo, told Reuters in Moscow on Thursday that the bank could use the exchange rate to fight against inflation, which is threatening to exceed the official 2008 target of 9.6 percent. (Reporting by Natalya Zinets, Writing by Ron Popeski)   \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 UKRAINE\b0 \highlight\uc2 -CBANK/\b \highlight22\uc2 INTERVENTION\b0 \highlight\uc2  (UPDATE 1)|LANGEN|ABN|M|D   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020080131e41v001tl\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
