\par\par \b \uc2 UPDATE 1- \highlight22\uc2 Ukraine hryvnia \highlight\uc2  hits 16 month low, cbank  \highlight22\uc2 intervenes \highlight\b0\par\par\uc2 292 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 22 Januar 2008\par 13:33\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2008 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 (Adds quotes)   \par \par \uc2 KIEV, Jan 22 (Reuters) - The Ukrainian \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  on the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market on Tuesday, selling dollars at 5.06 \b \highlight22\uc2 hryvnias\b0 \highlight\uc2  to support the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  which sank to a 16-month low, dealers said.   \par \par \uc2 They said the \b \highlight22\uc2 hryvnia\b0 \highlight\uc2  had weakened to 5.075, as foreign investors, hit by global market volatility, sought to retreat from Ukrainian \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  and stocks to gain dollars.   \par \par \uc2 Stocks around the world fell for the second day running, dragging down with them emerging markets as well as oil and commodity prices, over fears that the United States will descend into recession.   \par \par \uc2 "Almost everyone is buying (dollars) including foreigners and they could be making an exit from these kind of securities, as has been seen around the world," the dealer said.   \par \par \uc2 Dealers said large banks hit by the U.S. crisis would be wanting to amass dollars in markets they consider peripheral to shore up any losses.   \par \par \uc2 Ukraine's fledgling stock exchange market has fallen by several percentage points in the past three working days.   \par \par \uc2 "If foreigners are buying dollars, then for sure they are selling stocks for \b \highlight22\uc2 hryvnias\b0 \highlight\uc2 , buying dollars and coming out of our stock market," the dealer said.   \par \par \uc2 Another dealer said several large foreign banks muscled into the market to buy dollars in connection with natural gas and other energy trades.   \par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has defended the \b \highlight22\uc2 hryvnia\b0 \highlight\uc2  within a band of 5.00-5.06 to the dollar since August 2005. This is the first time it had \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  this year. (Reporting by Natalya Zinets; writing by Sabina Zawadzki; editing by Stephen Nisbet)   \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 UKRAINE\b0 \highlight\uc2 -\b \highlight22\uc2 HRYVNIA\b0 \highlight\uc2 /\b \highlight22\uc2 INTERVENTION\b0 \highlight\uc2  (UPDATE 1)|LANGEN|ABN|M|D|E|RBN|BNX|RNP|DNP|PTD|PMF   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020080122e41m0017d\par }\par \b \uc2 Zusammenfassung der Suche\b0\par \par  \trowd\trgaph15\trqc\trleft-15 \clvertalt\clbrdrt\brdrs\clbrdrl\brdrs\clbrdrb\brdrs\clbrdrr\brdrs \cellx2000\clvertalt\clbrdrt\brdrs\clbrdrl\brdrs\clbrdrb\brdrs\clbrdrr\brdrs \cellx9072\pard \ql \li0\ri0\widctlpar\intbl\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin0 \uc2 Text\cell \pard \ql \li0\ri0\widctlpar\intbl\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin0 \li50\uc2 (foreign exchange or fx or forex or currenc*) and (interven* or operation*) and (Ukraine near10 interven*) and (rst=trtw or rst=tprw or rst=tdjw) and (central bank or ministry of finance or treasury ministry or monetary authority) and hryvnia*\cell \pard \ql \li0\ri0\widctlpar\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin0 {  \trowd\trgaph15\trqc\trleft-15 \clvertalt\clbrdrt\brdrs\clbrdrl\brdrs\clbrdrb\brdrs\clbrdrr\brdrs \cellx2000\clvertalt\clbrdrt\brdrs\clbrdrl\brdrs\clbrdrb\brdrs\clbrdrr\brdrs \cellx9072\row } \trowd\trgaph15\trqc\trleft-15 \clvertalt\clbrdrt\brdrs\clbrdrl\brdrs\clbrdrb\brdrs\clbrdrr\brdrs \cellx2000\clvertalt\clbrdrt\brdrs\clbrdrl\brdrs\clbrdrb\brdrs\clbrdrr\brdrs \cellx9072\pard \ql \li0\ri0\widctlpar\intbl\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin0 \uc2 Datum\cell \pard \ql \li0\ri0\widctlpar\intbl\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin0 \li50\uc2